{
  "summary": "Configures the Nix Windows cross-compilation shell to build GCC with the POSIX thread model rather than the default MCF model, aligning CI with Guix release binaries. Target winpthreads headers and libraries are provided to GCC target libraries and the compiler wrapper without leaking into native host build tools. The PR also raises the Docker BuildKit step log limit to 5 MiB and logs the compiler configuration in CI before running tests.",
  "problem": "Nix Windows cross builds in CI used GCC's MCF thread model while Guix release binaries use POSIX threads, causing CI to test binaries with different threading runtimes and dependencies than production builds. In addition, default BuildKit per-step log limits truncated toolchain build output, obscuring configure flags.",
  "evidence": [
    "Linked issue #36314: 'windows: Thread model mismatch between Guix builds and CI'",
    "Commit 1d59d5ad25: 'Guix release binaries use the POSIX GCC thread model, but the pinned Nixpkgs cross compiler defaults to MCF. Select POSIX through the Nixpkgs threads hook so GCC and its target libraries agree.'"
  ],
